## Mapping from the DatoCMS UI

The tables below map every toggle of the "Create a new role" screen in the DatoCMS UI to its Terraform attribute. The DatoCMS API documents no default for any role attribute; this provider defaults every `can_*` flag to `false` and the build trigger, search index and inheritance lists to empty, so a role created with only `name` matches a role created in the UI with all toggles off. The four item/upload permission lists have no default: when omitted they are preserved as-is on the platform (see below).

### Project and environment management

| UI toggle | Terraform attribute | API default |
|---|---|---|
| Change project global properties | `can_edit_site` | not documented |
| Create/delete/rename sandbox environments | `can_manage_environments` | not documented |
| Promote sandbox environments to primary, rename all environments and manage maintenance mode | `can_promote_environments` | not documented |
| Create/edit roles and invite/remove collaborators | `can_manage_users` | not documented |
| Manage Single Sign-On settings | `can_manage_sso` | not documented |

### Automations and integrations

| UI toggle | Terraform attribute | API default |
|---|---|---|
| Create/edit webhooks | `can_manage_webhooks` | not documented |
| Create/edit API tokens | `can_manage_access_tokens` | not documented |
| Create/edit Build triggers | `can_manage_build_triggers` | not documented |
| Create/edit Search Indexes | `can_manage_search_indexes` | not documented |
| Perform Site Search API calls | `can_perform_site_search` | not documented |

### Activity tracking

| UI toggle | Terraform attribute | API default |
|---|---|---|
| Access deployment activity log | `can_access_build_events_log` | not documented |
| Access Search index activity log | `can_access_search_index_events_log` | not documented |
| Access to Audit log events | `can_access_audit_log` | not documented |

### Environment access

The two UI toggles "On primary environment" and "On sandbox environments" map to the single `environments_access` enum:

| On primary environment | On sandbox environments | `environments_access` |
|---|---|---|
| on | on | `all` |
| on | off | `primary_only` |
| off | on | `sandbox_only` |
| off | off | `none` |

`none` is typically used when the role inherits environment access from other roles.

### Environment permissions

| UI toggle | Terraform attribute | API default |
|---|---|---|
| Edit favicon, global SEO settings and no-index policy | `can_edit_favicon` | not documented |
| Customize all Content navigation items | `can_manage_menu` | not documented |
| Create/edit models and plugins | `can_edit_schema` | not documented |
| Change environment Locales & Timezone, Appearance, and run Available updates | `can_edit_environment` | not documented |
| Create/edit workflows | `can_manage_workflows` | not documented |
| Create/edit shared filters (both for models and the media area) | `can_manage_shared_filters` | not documented |
| Create/edit upload collections | `can_manage_upload_collections` | not documented |

### Rule-based permission panels

| UI panel | Terraform attribute | API default |
|---|---|---|
| Content permissions > Records and assets permissions (record rules) | `positive_item_type_permissions` / `negative_item_type_permissions` | not documented |
| Content permissions > Records and assets permissions (media rules) | `positive_upload_permissions` / `negative_upload_permissions` | not documented |
| Build permissions > Add new rule | `positive_build_trigger_permissions` / `negative_build_trigger_permissions` | not documented |
| Permissions to index with Search Indexes > Add new rule | `positive_search_index_permissions` / `negative_search_index_permissions` | not documented |
| Inherits permissions from (select) | `inherits_permissions_from` | not documented |

Negative permissions always take precedence over positive ones. On update the API replaces each declared permission array wholesale; there is no merging.

### Preserving content permission rules (managing only the role form)

The four item/upload permission lists (`positive_item_type_permissions`, `negative_item_type_permissions`, `positive_upload_permissions`, `negative_upload_permissions`) are special: when they are omitted from the configuration they are left untouched on the platform. Terraform then manages only the "first screen" of the role (the `can_*` flags, `environments_access`, build trigger and search index rules, and inheritance) while the record/asset rules keep being edited in the DatoCMS UI. This also works with `terraform import`: import a role, declare only the first-screen attributes, and the plan shows no changes while the content rules stay as they are.

Declare a list, even as `[]`, to have Terraform manage it (an explicit `[]` clears it).

Note: the DatoCMS API requires the positive and negative halves of each pair (item type, upload) to be sent together. When only one half of a pair is declared, the provider sends the other half too: with its current platform value on update (still effectively preserved) and as `[]` on create.

